# Suppressions for the docker image scan (scripts/trivy-scan-image).
#
# Each entry needs a preceding `# remove_after: YYYY_MM_DD`; scripts/trivy-check-expiry
# fails the build once that date passes, so a stale suppression can't outlive its fix.

# pip's own vendored dependencies, reported via pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json (a
# CycloneDX SBOM that trivy parses as installed python packages). These are not
# importable site-packages distributions — nothing but pip resolves them — so they
# can only move when pip re-vendors upstream, not via `pip install`.
#
# CVE-2025-47273 is a path traversal in setuptools.package_index.PackageIndex. pip
# vendors only pkg_resources out of setuptools 70.3.0; package_index.py is not in
# the image at all, so the vulnerable code is absent. The real site-packages
# setuptools is pinned >= 78.1.1 in base.Dockerfile and py.Dockerfile, which is what
# guards against an actual vulnerable install.
#
# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 is an out-of-bounds read in msgpack 1.1.2 on Unpacker reuse.
# pip reaches it through cachecontrol when deserialising its own HTTP cache, so
# triggering it needs an already-corrupted local pip cache. Fixed in msgpack 1.2.1,
# pending a pip re-vendor.
# remove_after: 2026_12_01
CVE-2025-47273
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
